>What is its effects?

Manyfold. There is a MB FAQ IIRC. Let's see:

1) It gives you magic resistance. Not a big deal for a wizard, but
a really good thing for most other classes.

2) It catches curses. So later in the game when you have lichs and
nagas and named demons throwing curses at you to curse your stuff,
MB will deflect most of them.

3) It does many effects when it hits monsters. This includes:
cancellation
stunning
probing (get monster stats and items carried)
scare
confusion

4) It can engrave Elbereth in 1 turn and it doesn't get dull.

5) It can safely be enchanted up to +7, though at +7 it loses most
of the abilities listed in #3 above.

In short it's your best friend. Wield it and use it for the forseeable
future.

>How rare is it to obtain it the way i did?

Not rare at all. MB is the first artifact weapon given to wizards. So
if you simply sacrifice and pray enough, you'll eventually get it.

Like I said before... Congratulations!

